msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/02-vector-addition.md:107
msgid ""
"Calling `add(z, x, y)` launches an 8×8×1 grid from `z`'s host-side "
"partition. Each of the 64 tile blocks processes a 4×4 chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/02-vector-addition.md:112
msgid "The Kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/02-vector-addition.md:114
msgid ""
"fn add<const S: [i32; 2]>(\n"
"    z: &mut Tensor<f32, S>,       // Output sub-tensor (4×4)\n"
"    x: &Tensor<f32, {[-1, -1]}>,  // Full input tensor\n"
"    y: &Tensor<f32, {[-1, -1]}>   // Full input tensor\n"
") {\n"
"    let tile_x = x.load_like(z);\n"
"    let tile_y = y.load_like(z);\n"
"    z.store(tile_x + tile_y);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/02-vector-addition.md:126
msgid ""
"`x.load_like(z)` loads a tile from `x` using the same tile shape (`S`=4×4) "
"and coordinates (tile thread id) as `z`."
msgstr ""

